{
  "$comment": "Whether a plugin's CHALLENGED at `url` is offered to the viewer as a browser check, on both hosts: `refusal` is null where it is, and otherwise the rule it failed, worded identically because a television logs it and `run` and `doctor` print it. `reached` is the sites the call's yonto.fetch reached, on any hop. test/browser-check.test.js walks it through src/browser-check.js and BrowserChecksRecordTest through BrowserChecks.kt. See docs/design/2026-09-23-a-challenge-the-viewer-clears.md, *How a plugin asks*.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "why": "a url-form check at the site the call reached is offered",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [
          "site.test"
        ],
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "url": "https://site.test/"
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://site.test/list?page=3",
      "reached": [
        "https://site.test"
      ],
      "refusal": null
    },
    {
      "why": "a fromConfig check covers any public https site a hostsFromConfig plugin reached",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [],
        "hostsFromConfig": true,
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://catalog.test/vod",
      "reached": [
        "https://catalog.test"
      ],
      "refusal": null
    },
    {
      "why": "a site the call did not reach is an accident, not a check",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [],
        "hostsFromConfig": true,
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://moved-off.test/",
      "reached": [
        "https://catalog.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "yonto.fetch did not reach it in this call"
    },
    {
      "why": "a plugin that declares no check gets none",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [
          "site.test"
        ],
        "capabilities": []
      },
      "url": "https://site.test/",
      "reached": [
        "https://site.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "no browserCheck in the manifest covers it"
    },
    {
      "why": "a url-form check covers its own site and no other",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [
          "site.test",
          "other.test"
        ],
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "url": "https://site.test/"
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://other.test/",
      "reached": [
        "https://other.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "no browserCheck in the manifest covers it"
    },
    {
      "why": "a fromConfig check on a plugin without hostsFromConfig is no check at all",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [
          "site.test"
        ],
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://site.test/",
      "reached": [
        "https://site.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "no browserCheck in the manifest covers it"
    },
    {
      "why": "a clearance on the wire is a clearance given away, whatever the manifest covers",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [],
        "hostsFromConfig": true,
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "http://catalog.test/",
      "reached": [
        "http://catalog.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "it is not https"
    },
    {
      "why": "a check on the viewer's own network is not a thing a site asks for",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [],
        "hostsFromConfig": true,
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://192.168.1.1/",
      "reached": [
        "https://192.168.1.1"
      ],
      "refusal": "it is a private address"
    },
    {
      "why": "the site of the plugin's cookieLogin already has a host-held credential",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [],
        "hostsFromConfig": true,
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "cookieLogin",
            "url": "https://login.test/"
          },
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://login.test/",
      "reached": [
        "https://login.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "it is the site of the plugin's cookieLogin"
    },
    {
      "why": "what the plugin raised is not a URL",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [],
        "hostsFromConfig": true,
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "Just a moment...",
      "reached": [
        "https://catalog.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "it is not a URL"
    },
    {
      "why": "a URL carrying a user name and password is not opened, as yonto.fetch will not send one",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [],
        "hostsFromConfig": true,
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://user:pw@catalog.test/",
      "reached": [
        "https://catalog.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "it carries a user name or password"
    },
    {
      "why": "a user name alone is refused the same way",
      "manifest": {
        "allowedHosts": [],
        "hostsFromConfig": true,
        "capabilities": [
          {
            "type": "browserCheck",
            "fromConfig": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "url": "https://user@catalog.test/",
      "reached": [
        "https://catalog.test"
      ],
      "refusal": "it carries a user name or password"
    }
  ]
}
